<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2011/08/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>NtObjectManager</id>
    <version>2.0.1</version>
    <authors>James Forshaw</authors>
    <owners>Google LLC.</owners>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <licenseUrl>http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.html</licenseUrl>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/googleprojectzero/sandbox-attacksurface-analysis-tools</projectUrl>
    <description>This module adds a provider and cmdlets to access the NT object manager namespace.</description>
    <releaseNotes>2.0.1.
--------
* Improvements to RPC tooling.

NOTE: This version is a major refactor of the code. Scripts which only use exposed PowerShell commands
should work when upgrading from v1 to v2, however if you use internal APIs it will almost certainly
not work due to refactoring and renaming. Going forward it's recommended to not rely on internal 
APIs to work across releases.</releaseNotes>
